From c64ea6425928b1cee978caae96f67d15456e5a0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Wed, 08 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] xenlib: guard xu console against unmanaged (toolstack-introduced) domains


`xu console <domid>` on a toolstack-introduced guest (a DomU/DomA created by
the DomD `xl` toolstack) crashed the whole Zephyr Dom0 (NULL/unmapped-ring
dereference -> CPU exception -> "Halting system").

Such a guest is tracked in domain_list via xs_introduce() (sys_dlist_append),
but its console ring is never mapped by this Dom0: xen_init_domain_console()
runs only in the Dom0-driven domain_create() path (xen_start_domain_console),
so domain->console.intf stays NULL (the domain struct is memset to 0). The
attach handler only checked !domain and domain->f_dom0less, not the console-
init state, so it armed the shell bypass and the display thread then
dereferenced the unmapped ring and faulted.

Guard xen_attach_domain_console(): after taking &domain->console, refuse the
attach when console->intf is NULL (return -ENODEV) and point the operator at
the owning toolstack (`xl console` on the driver domain). A Dom0-created
domain has intf mapped (non-NULL), so a valid attach is unaffected. Also
release the get_domain() borrow (put_domain) on the f_dom0less early return,
which previously leaked it.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-4-8
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/xen-console-srv/src/xen_console.c b/xen-console-srv/src/xen_console.c
index 6022114..6bef87b 100644
--- a/xen-console-srv/src/xen_console.c
+++ b/xen-console-srv/src/xen_console.c
@@ -477,10 +477,24 @@ int xen_attach_domain_console(const struct shell *shell,
 
 	if (domain->f_dom0less) {
 		LOG_ERR("dom0less domain#%u console operation not supported", domain->domid);
+		put_domain(domain);
 		return -ENOTSUP;
 	}
 
 	console = &domain->console;
+	/* A toolstack-introduced guest (e.g. DomU/DomA created by the DomD
+	 * xl toolstack) is tracked in domain_list via xs_introduce() but its console
+	 * ring was never mapped by this Dom0 (xen_init_domain_console() runs only in
+	 * the Dom0-driven domain_create() path, so console.intf stays NULL). Attaching
+	 * would arm the shell bypass and then dereference the unmapped ring, faulting
+	 * the whole Zephyr Dom0. Refuse gracefully and point at the owning toolstack. */
+	if (!console->intf) {
+		shell_error(shell,
+			    "domain#%u console is not managed by Dom0 (use the owning toolstack, e.g. 'xl console %u' on the driver domain)",
+			    domain->domid, domain->domid);
+		put_domain(domain);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
 	k_mutex_lock(&global_console_lock, K_FOREVER);
 	if (current_console) {
 		/* Actually, this should never happen */
